{"title":"Hardware Design Engineer Roadmap","role":"Hardware Design Engineer","summary":"A Hardware Design Engineer designs, simulates, tests, debugs and improves electronic circuits and systems. The role can span digital logic, analog circuits, PCB design, embedded hardware, FPGA/ASIC development and hardware verification.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 of UG","Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Electronics & Communication Engineering (ECE)","Timeline assumption":"Four-year B.Tech/B.E. beginning in 2026 and graduating around 2030."},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Hardware Design Engineer is directly aligned with ECE."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Hardware/Embedded Intern → Junior Hardware Design Engineer with circuit, PCB and embedded-system projects."},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"PCB design, embedded hardware, FPGA, ASIC/RTL, analog or mixed-signal design."},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Hardware Design Engineer → Hardware/Design Lead or specialist engineer."},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Hardware architecture, semiconductor systems, advanced verification, edge AI and hardware-software co-design."}],"sections":[{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from (free unless noted)","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 · Sem 1"},{"text":"Circuit fundamentals + C programming"},{"text":"NPTEL · Arduino Documentation","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Simulate basic circuits and build 3 microcontroller experiments"},{"text":"Analytical thinking, execution"}],[{"text":"Year 1 · Sem 2"},{"text":"Digital electronics + Boolean logic"},{"text":"MIT OpenCourseWare","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/"},{"text":"Build counters, multiplexers, registers and logic circuits"},{"text":"Analytical thinking"}],[{"text":"Year 2 · Sem 1"},{"text":"Microcontrollers + embedded C"},{"text":"Arm Developer · Arduino","url":"https://developer.arm.com/"},{"text":"Sensor-based embedded project with documented firmware"},{"text":"Digital literacy, execution"}],[{"text":"Year 2 · Sem 2"},{"text":"PCB design + electronics prototyping"},{"text":"KiCad Documentation","url":"https://docs.kicad.org/"},{"text":"Design and fabricate a two-layer PCB"},{"text":"Creativity, execution"}],[{"text":"Year 3 · Sem 1"},{"text":"FPGA/HDL or advanced embedded hardware"},{"text":"AMD Vivado documentation · Verilog/SystemVerilog resources","url":"https://docs.amd.com/"},{"text":"Implement and test an RTL design on FPGA"},{"text":"Analytical thinking, technical depth"}],[{"text":"Year 3 · Sem 2"},{"text":"Hardware verification + internship"},{"text":"RISC-V International · GitHub Skills","url":"https://riscv.org/"},{"text":"Verification project + internship experience"},{"text":"Communication, ownership"}],[{"text":"Year 4 · Sem 1"},{"text":"Specialised hardware design"},{"text":"Texas Instruments training resources · Intel FPGA documentation","url":"https://training.ti.com/"},{"text":"Advanced PCB/FPGA/embedded hardware project"},{"text":"Strategic thinking"}],[{"text":"Year 4 · Sem 2"},{"text":"Industry-ready capstone"},{"text":"GitHub","url":"https://github.com/"},{"text":"Complete hardware design package: schematic + PCB + firmware + test report"},{"text":"Leadership, execution"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"4-year honours variant"},{"type":"p","text":"Use the additional honours year for advanced work in ASIC/SoC design, FPGA architecture, mixed-signal electronics, RF hardware, semiconductor device modelling, hardware security or edge-AI accelerators."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation options"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Learn from","Senior role it leads to"],"rows":[[{"text":"PCB & Embedded Hardware"},{"text":"Analog/digital circuits, KiCad, MCUs, sensors"},{"text":"KiCad · Arm Developer","url":"https://www.kicad.org/"},{"text":"Senior Hardware Engineer"}],[{"text":"FPGA/RTL"},{"text":"Verilog/SystemVerilog, FPGA, timing, verification"},{"text":"AMD FPGA documentation","url":"https://docs.amd.com/"},{"text":"FPGA Design Lead"}],[{"text":"ASIC/VLSI"},{"text":"RTL, synthesis, STA, verification"},{"text":"RISC-V International","url":"https://riscv.org/"},{"text":"RTL/ASIC Design Lead"}],[{"text":"Embedded Systems"},{"text":"MCU, C/C++, RTOS, peripherals"},{"text":"Arm Developer","url":"https://developer.arm.com/"},{"text":"Embedded Hardware Lead"}],[{"text":"Edge AI Hardware"},{"text":"Embedded systems, accelerators, AI inference"},{"text":"TensorFlow Lite documentation","url":"https://ai.google.dev/edge/litert"},{"text":"Edge AI Hardware Architect"}],[{"text":"Mixed-Signal"},{"text":"Analog, digital, ADC/DAC, signal integrity"},{"text":"Texas Instruments training","url":"https://training.ti.com/"},{"text":"Mixed-Signal Design Lead"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Evolve and stay relevant, 2035–2046"},{"type":"p","text":"Hardware engineering is increasingly connected with software, AI accelerators, semiconductor design, edge computing and energy efficiency. Develop expertise beyond circuit design: hardware-software co-design, verification, security, thermal/power considerations, high-speed interfaces and manufacturability."}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Government"},{"type":"table","header":["Route","Who can apply","Pay and cost","Link"],"rows":[[{"text":"ISRO student opportunities"},{"text":"Depends on academic programme and current notification"},{"text":"Pay/allowance: check the official site"},{"text":"ISRO Careers","url":"https://www.isro.gov.in/Careers.html"}],[{"text":"DRDO internships/training"},{"text":"Depends on laboratory, discipline and current notification"},{"text":"Pay: check the official site"},{"text":"DRDO","url":"https://www